      "writtenOn": "2021-10-04T22:37:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To test BC1.2, you need to test host mode and client mode.\nTo test client mode, connect a USB-A cable to the DUTs type C using an A to C adapter.  You can verify the DUT starts charging using \"chgsup\".  Depending on what you connect to the USB-A cable, the DUT should charge at 500mA or 1.5A.\nTo test host mode, connect a non-PD device to the type C of the DUT.  The DUT should provide 5V power to the connected device.\n\nYou should also see debug messages from the pi3usb9201 driver indicating if it enabled host mode.",
      "parentUuid": "0d64cbe1_4b5b8996",
